<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>Deutsche Welle: DW.com - Sports</title><subtitle type="html">Deutsche Welle: DW.com - Sports</subtitle><id>https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-sports</id><updated>2026-09-17T19:47:54Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss-en-sports" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.dw.com/s-8171?maca=en-rss-en-sports-1027-xml-mrss" /><link rel="via" href="https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-sports" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>Klopp wants Germany's football team to 'reclaim the flag'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:057736f0b24fd2dd61dde9254b14a2640f7c867b2712f312a03d4ecaa0741b0f</id><updated>2026-09-17T19:47:54Z</updated><published>2026-09-17T11:41:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/klopp-wants-germany-s-football-team-to-reclaim-the-flag/a-79307610--57ff88db5991.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/klopp-wants-germany-s-football-team-to-reclaim-the-flag/a-79307610?maca=en-rss-en-sports-1027-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Jürgen Klopp, Germany's new head coach, says he wants his team to reclaim pride in being German after recent political developments.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Jürgen Klopp's first Germany squad includes 44 players</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:551d1b650f12c757eb77a028f394d92f0ffdb8fbe0b65d8b7d298434702c0cee</id><updated>2026-09-17T19:47:02Z</updated><published>2026-09-17T08:50:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/j_rgen-klopp-s-first-germany-squad-includes-44-players/a-79289254--9874c23792d0.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/jürgen-klopp-s-first-germany-squad-includes-44-players/a-79289254?maca=en-rss-en-sports-1027-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Germany's new head coach Jürgen Klopp has named a huge squad for his first four games, splitting them into two groups. A host of new faces is included.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>After Neuer: Who will be Germany's new No. 1 goalkeeper?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ce415e00693ef86d0fdbbcbc5ae28a0833ee1b6d7d24f3f1d1f01a1c0f5c93d3</id><updated>2026-09-17T19:47:02Z</updated><published>2026-09-16T14:25:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/after-neuer-who-will-be-germany-s-new-no-1-goalkeeper/a-79276377--1d35484fc587.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/after-neuer-who-will-be-germany-s-new-no-1-goalkeeper/a-79276377?maca=en-rss-en-sports-1027-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Following Manuel Neuer's retirement, there are many candidates to succeed him, but which goalkeeper will Jürgen Klopp choose? What factors will play a role? And will Neuer's future have an indirect influence?</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Jürgen Klopp and Germany: A partnership long in the making</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e377a1c0b00404e0269d6e81c6eb54314c50456f61abc0bdb352f78df165203e</id><updated>2026-09-17T19:47:02Z</updated><published>2026-07-24T09:04:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/j_rgen-klopp-and-germany-a-partnership-long-in-the-making/a-77805100--2614f917074b.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/jürgen-klopp-and-germany-a-partnership-long-in-the-making/a-77805100?maca=en-rss-en-sports-1027-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">In one of the worst-kept secrets in football, the former Dortmund and Liverpool boss has been named head coach of the German men's national team.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Alexander Ovechkin backs Putin party in campaign video</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:4af5867e016c652ec522fc850a60f9374eac5174463573954c932ca19e349e1b</id><updated>2026-09-17T19:47:02Z</updated><published>2026-09-17T16:02:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/alexander-ovechkin-backs-putin-party-in-campaign-video/a-79277772--a8049deceb76.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/alexander-ovechkin-backs-putin-party-in-campaign-video/a-79277772?maca=en-rss-en-sports-1027-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Ice hockey legend Alexander Ovechkin has lent Vladimir Putin's party a helping hand in its parliamentary election campaign. That's in keeping with a pattern of support by an athlete who claims not to be political.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Women's Basketball World Cup: Can Germany harness a boom?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:594c7e668cc578b49ffdb47d88eeeb4441bddddcf4fe70eba4586b36ff0d5bc1</id><updated>2026-09-17T19:47:02Z</updated><published>2026-09-14T15:07:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/women-s-basketball-world-cup-can-germany-harness-a-boom/a-79263602--77d972e02866.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/women-s-basketball-world-cup-can-germany-harness-a-boom/a-79263602?maca=en-rss-en-sports-1027-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Germany thrilled fans at the Women's Basketball World Cup. But even if this sparked a boom in the women's game, the infrastructure simply isn't ready for it.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Germany's Zverev wins US Open in golden year</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:435bc764fb1c3794bbf2c8a8b578e6e0a3971b32c3a0dbed1e0cabd547f77da4</id><updated>2026-09-17T19:47:02Z</updated><published>2026-09-13T22:03:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-s-zverev-wins-us-open-in-golden-year/a-79212706--d962ccd6a0c8.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-s-zverev-wins-us-open-in-golden-year/a-79212706?maca=en-rss-en-sports-1027-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Alexander Zverev has won the US Open for the first time, defeating Ben Shelton in the final. It is Zverev's second Grand Slam win of 2026 after a long wait for his first title, but controversy still hangs over him.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>LIV Golf in financial turmoil: What's next for the sport?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ae7c517db4cd66741c97baf0df8a245948df841c3c59b972a398ea612d6e4693</id><updated>2026-09-17T19:47:02Z</updated><published>2026-09-09T11:16:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/liv-golf-in-financial-turmoil-what-s-next-for-the-sport/a-79199569--378367d5fd0c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/liv-golf-in-financial-turmoil-what-s-next-for-the-sport/a-79199569?maca=en-rss-en-sports-1027-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Six months after Saudi Arabia pulled funding from the breakaway organization, LIV Golf have filed for bankruptcy protection. Several of the world's best players signed on to LIV, so where does that leave golf?</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Elversberg: Bundesliga newcomers from tiny town make waves</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:699308edde6c932fb314b89a99e4cc526b651a6dac5ffeed98c49db724e9e6e6</id><updated>2026-09-17T19:47:02Z</updated><published>2026-09-08T06:47:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/elversberg-bundesliga-newcomers-from-tiny-town-make-waves/a-77194483--9d72d35ebb6f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/elversberg-bundesliga-newcomers-from-tiny-town-make-waves/a-77194483?maca=en-rss-en-sports-1027-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A team from a small southwestern German town of just 7,000 inhabitants made history by sealing promotion to become the 59th club to play in the Bundesliga. Elversberg has got off to a memorable start.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Egg freezing in women's football: Choice or pressure?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8771eb3f942cdfdb8c736d245914e9087ab2a43c60b33f2ee6e5dd31f3642445</id><updated>2026-09-17T19:47:02Z</updated><published>2026-09-08T06:45:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/egg-freezing-in-women-s-football-choice-or-pressure/a-79145259--8a56ba698069.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/egg-freezing-in-women-s-football-choice-or-pressure/a-79145259?maca=en-rss-en-sports-1027-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Spain's football federation is set to join a handful of clubs in paying for female players to freeze their eggs. Experts have welfare concerns.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>New study shows German football remains male-dominated</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c5d2e59d5fe1099cdd00c6fe37421459febd4fda9cf7023737846b267ded4d2e</id><updated>2026-09-17T19:47:02Z</updated><published>2026-08-27T13:53:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/new-study-shows-german-football-remains-male-dominated/a-78532569--b9ee319bf21e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/new-study-shows-german-football-remains-male-dominated/a-78532569?maca=en-rss-en-sports-1027-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The top leagues of German football remain a largely male environment. A new study reveals that only seven clubs have women in upper management levels.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>The new Bundesliga season is here, but has the glow gone?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:76fb767ab323116e82279d7805b591e0c479c4c258c72b6511ef88a26bb63322</id><updated>2026-09-17T19:47:02Z</updated><published>2026-08-24T14:54:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/the-new-bundesliga-season-is-here-but-has-the-glow-gone/a-78062032--f578ab52d735.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/the-new-bundesliga-season-is-here-but-has-the-glow-gone/a-78062032?maca=en-rss-en-sports-1027-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Another Bundesliga season arrives, but are the golden years of Germany's top football league already over, and what can it do to change its course?</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry></feed>
